    <string name="stats_auc_title">What does AUC mean?</string>
    <string name="stats_auc_text">AUC tells how often the model scores a real find higher than a random comparison (another place or another day of the season). It needs no threshold and is fair even for rare events.</string>
    <string name="stats_auc_05">0.5 = guessing (coin flip)</string>
    <string name="stats_auc_07">0.7 = good for such a hard task</string>
    <string name="stats_auc_10">1.0 = perfect</string>
    <string name="stats_auc_note">Finds appear where and when people walk in the forest, so the numbers are only an approximate estimate.</string>
